# The size budgets for PureMouse.app (installed) and the release dmg, checked by scripts/check-
# size.sh
# (release.sh runs it on both, so CI does).
# Raising one is a reviewed change: say in the pull request what grew and why.
#
# Each budget is the measured size plus 15%, rounded up to the next 0.1 MB (1 MB = 1,000,000
# bytes), plus the allowance below while there is one (none after a release is measured), and the
# README's Download row quotes the measured sizes rounded to 0.1 MB. A test
# (scripts/tests/test_size.zsh) holds the budgets and the README to the measurements, so
# changing one of them means changing the measurement here.
#
# Measured 2026-11-03 from the published 0.5.1 release: `PureMouse-0.5.1.dmg` as downloaded from
# GitHub (its SHA256SUMS checked), and the universal PureMouse.app inside it, mounted read-only and
# summed as check-size.sh sums it. The installed figure sums the bytes of every path, so the nested
# apps' hard-linked Assets.car (one inode, three names) counts three times; only the dmg holds it
# once (`du` puts the same app at 8.6 MB).
INSTALLED_MEASURED_BYTES=12429914
DMG_MEASURED_BYTES=4948496
#
# Allowance for mouse v2 (#149), settings recovery (#164) and the #146 batch, cleared when 0.6.0 is
# measured. A budget
# is the measured size plus 15%, rounded up to 0.1 MB, plus an allowance when a change in flight
# takes CI's largest figure past that: the overshoot rounded up to 0.1 MB, so the cap keeps under
# 0.1 MB of headroom over what CI measures. The installed figure is CI's on ca8b65b, the
# compatibility job's Xcode 26 universal build (the test job's release dry run measured 14,729,101);
# the dmg figure is the test job's release dry run on 332e2e5 (run 41633211845), 5,971,858 bytes.
# Main 43dcb6f measured 13,946,142 installed and 5,541,062 dmg; 6ea7319 (#149) 14,516,018 (+569,876)
# and 5,813,199 (+272,137); #164 14,884,546 installed (+368,528 on 6ea7319) and 5,971,858 dmg
# (+158,659).
# The #149 growth is code: the device card, the app page and the other Settings panes (about
# 0.5 MB in the Settings helper, 0.05 MB in the menu bar app, local Swift 6.4 builds against main),
# plus the eight device PDFs (37 KB, in the Settings helper only). The #164 growth is code too, from
# a local stripped arm64 release build against main 62b4eea (the universal app carries it twice):
# the daemon +87 KB (applied state and the retry rules in Session, timeout leases and reply
# observers in the HID++ endpoint, Easy-Switch hosts and firmware, and their status fields), the
# menu bar app +51 KB (status text, the not-applied rows and the detail line), the Settings helper
# +84 KB (the device rows, About This Mouse and the notification row). No debug code or dev hook is
# in a release binary (checked by strings), and nothing is a large table or literal; the one cheap
# trim, a needless sort of the reply observers, is made. test_size.zsh holds the arithmetic.
# #167 (media keys and Middle Click) 14,933,970 installed on fbd3c1e (+49,424 on #164): the new
# Action cases, AuxKey media keys, the held middle button and their catalog rows.
# #168 (pointer pane and the disclosure rows) 6,001,667 dmg on 436d214 (+29,809 on #164's figure);
# installed stays under #167's.
# #174 (Undo and Redo in Settings) 15,051,666 installed on 8ee74c3 (+66,624 on #166's 14,985,042):
# the undo history, its step names and the file-level replay in ConfigStore.
# #172 (Pointer Speed for each mouse, the paused icon) 15,118,201 installed on d07d022's
# compatibility build (+66,535 on #174's 15,051,666): the per-mouse preset sections, the scope in
# ShowRequest and the cut slash.
# #177 (action packs) 15,322,232 installed on c905f14's compatibility build (+204,031 on #172's
# 15,118,201): the picker's pack sections and search, ActionPackCatalog, and the 38 KB catalogue in
# the Settings helper; about 57 KB of code per architecture. 6,139,469 dmg (+75,060 on 6,064,409).
# #176 (click, double-click and hold) 15,521,448 installed on 92cfdf4's compatibility build
# (+199,216 on #177's 15,322,232): trigger tables in PureMouseKit, which all three binaries link,
# the daemon's press plans and deadlines, and Settings' trigger rows; per architecture about 48 KB
# daemon, 32 KB Settings, 32 KB menu.
# #176 6,254,464 dmg on 92cfdf4 (+114,995 on #177's 6,139,469).
INSTALLED_CI_BYTES=15521448
DMG_CI_BYTES=6254464
INSTALLED_EXTRA_BYTES=1300000
DMG_EXTRA_BYTES=600000
INSTALLED_MAX_BYTES=15600000
DMG_MAX_BYTES=6300000
